From: adesh chaudhari <superbhel7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:28:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat(frontend): seat-hold confirm flow with a live
 countdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

YG-6 — the most important gap in the old flow.

POST /api/bookings does not complete a booking: it places a 10-minute hold with
the seats already decremented and expiresAt set. The mock flow went straight
from ticket selection to a success screen, so every booking it produced would
have been swept to EXPIRED minutes later with the seats released.

BookingConfirmPage counts down from expiresAt, calls /confirm, and offers an
explicit /cancel that releases the seats immediately rather than waiting out
the sweeper. It also renders the terminal states, so a refreshed or expired
hold explains itself instead of offering a button that can no longer work.

BookingSuccessPage is now reachable only after confirm returns CONFIRMED, and
its hardcoded fallback booking is gone — it was rendering a confirmation for a
booking that did not exist whenever it had no state.
